{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Go up this way in the Negev.</b> Go up this way in the Negev. It is known that Egypt is south of the land of Israel, as I explained in the book of Daniel. The proof is that the latitude of Egypt is less than thirty degrees and the latitude of Jerusalem is thirty-three, and the wilderness of Paran is south of the land of Egypt. Now the meaning of \"in the Negev\" is not the south of the camp, but rather its meaning is in the south of the land of Canaan. The proof is Hebron, which belongs to Judah, and Scripture says, Judah shall stand on its border from the south."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:27.375640222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}